@backend_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000
@tickets = {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/tickets

### Baseline — all tickets, default sort (newest first), default page size
GET {{tickets}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Pagination — page 1, small page size (proves limit works)
GET {{tickets}}?page=1&limit=5
Accept: application/json

###

### Pagination — page 2 (proves offset; should show rows 6–10 of the seed)
GET {{tickets}}?page=2&limit=5
Accept: application/json

###

### Limit clamp — asking for 500 should cap at 100 (MaxPageSize)
GET {{tickets}}?limit=500
Accept: application/json

###

### Status — single value
GET {{tickets}}?status=open
Accept: application/json

###

### Status — multi-select (SQL WHERE status IN (...))
GET {{tickets}}?status=open,in_progress
Accept: application/json

###

### Status — the in_progress underscore-parsing case specifically
GET {{tickets}}?status=in_progress
Accept: application/json

###

### Priority — single value
GET {{tickets}}?priority=urgent
Accept: application/json

###

### Priority — multi-select
GET {{tickets}}?priority=high,urgent
Accept: application/json

###

### Category — single category by id (seeded: cat_it_hardware, cat_it_access, cat_hr_payroll)
GET {{tickets}}?category=cat_it_access
Accept: application/json

###

### Assignee — unassigned (AssigneeId IS NULL)
GET {{tickets}}?assignee=unassigned
Accept: application/json

###

### Assignee — specific moderator by id (seeded: usr_sam, usr_priya)
GET {{tickets}}?assignee=usr_sam
Accept: application/json

###

### Assignee — "me" (currently a no-op until auth; should behave like no filter)
GET {{tickets}}?assignee=me
Accept: application/json

###

### Search — free text across subject/description
GET {{tickets}}?search=vpn
Accept: application/json

###

### Search — no matches (proves the "no tickets match" empty state)
GET {{tickets}}?search=zzzznotfound
Accept: application/json

###

### Sort — by priority descending (severity order, proves int storage sorts right)
GET {{tickets}}?sort=priority desc
Accept: application/json

###

### Sort — by createdAt ascending (oldest first)
GET {{tickets}}?sort=createdAt
Accept: application/json

###

### Sort — multi-field (priority desc, then newest first within each)
GET {{tickets}}?sort=priority,createdAt
Accept: application/json

###

### Sort — invalid field should return 400 Problem (whitelist rejection)
GET {{tickets}}?sort=passwordHash
Accept: application/json

###

### Combined — the "real" moderator-queue query: open+in_progress, high+urgent, unassigned, newest first
GET {{tickets}}?status=open,in_progress&priority=high,urgent&assignee=unassigned&sort=priority desc,createdAt desc&page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

###
### Ticket detail — valid id (grab a real tkt_ id from GET /api/tickets first)
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### Ticket detail — this ticket has comments in the seed? (thread should be ordered oldest-first)
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### Ticket detail — non-existent id returns 404 Problem
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_does_not_exist
Accept: application/json

###

### Ticket detail — garbage id (not even a tkt_ prefix) still 404, not 500
GET {{tickets}}/garbage
Accept: application/json

###

### Round-trip — create a ticket, then fetch it by the returned id
# 1) run this, copy "id" from the 201 response body / Location header
POST {{tickets}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Detail endpoint smoke test",
  "description": "Created to verify GET by id returns the same shape.",
  "priority": "high",
  "categoryId": "cat_it_access"
}

###

# 2) paste the id from step 1 here
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_PASTE_ID_FROM_CREATE
Accept: application/json

###

### Add comment — valid (paste a real tkt_ id; then re-run GET detail to see the thread)
POST {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Tried reconnecting from a different network, same failure."
}

###

### Add comment — second one, to prove oldest-first ordering in the detail thread
POST {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Escalating — this is blocking the whole team."
}

###

### Add comment — empty body returns 400 with field-level errors
POST {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": ""
}

###

### Add comment — non-existent ticket returns 404 (path resource missing, not 400)
POST {{tickets}}/tkt_does_not_exist/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "This should never be stored."
}

###

### Verify the thread — run after the two valid comments above
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### PATCH — change status only (priority + assignee must stay untouched)
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

###

### PATCH — change priority only
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priority": "urgent"
}

###

### PATCH — assign to a moderator (seed: usr_sam, usr_priya)
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assigneeId": "usr_sam"
}

###

### PATCH — all three at once
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "resolved",
  "priority": "high",
  "assigneeId": "usr_priya"
}

###

### PATCH — empty body (no-op, should 200 and change nothing, no UpdatedAt bump)
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

###

### PATCH — invalid status enum, should 400 (from the JSON reader, not FluentValidation)
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "banana"
}

###

### PATCH — snake_case enum. FAILS with 400 today; passes only if the snake_case
### naming policy is added to JsonStringEnumConverter in Program.cs
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_progress"
}

###

### PATCH — non-existent ticket, should 404
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_does_not_exist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "open"
}

###

### Verify partial-update: PATCH only status, then GET — priority/assignee unchanged
PATCH {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "closed"
}

###

GET {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0
Accept: application/json

###
### DELETE — soft-delete a ticket (grab a real tkt_ id first). Expect 204.
DELETE {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID

###

### Verify it's gone from detail — expect 404
GET {{tickets}}/tkt_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### Verify it's gone from the list — this id should NOT appear in data[]
GET {{tickets}}?limit=100
Accept: application/json

###

### DELETE again — already soft-deleted, expect 404 (not a second 204)
DELETE {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0

###

### DELETE non-existent — expect 404
DELETE {{tickets}}/tkt_01a068fc-1dbf-7f35-81c9-63af302303f0

###

### List categories — now returns { data, pagination }, name-sorted by default.
### NOTE: every request in this file predates auth and will 401 — the tokened
### versions of these live in rbac.http.
GET {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a category — expect 201
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "IT - Software"
}

###

### Create duplicate — expect 409 Conflict
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "IT - Software"
}

###

### Create duplicate, different case — should STILL 409 (case-insensitive)
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "it - software"
}

###

### Empty name — expect 400 (validation)
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

###

### Verify new category is filterable on tickets (use its returned id)
GET {{tickets}}?category=cat_hr_payroll
Accept: application/json

###